.TH "SPEECHRECOGNITION.RESULT_EVENT" "3JS" "July 28, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
SpeechRecognition.result_event \- SpeechRecognition: result event
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]result\f[B]\f[R] event of the Web Speech API is fired
when the speech recognition service returns a result \(em a word or
phrase has been positively recognized and this has been communicated
back to the app
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in methods like \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R], or set
an event handler property.
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqresult\(dq, (event) => { })

onresult = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
A \f[CR]SpeechRecognitionEvent\f[R].
Inherits from \f[CR]Event\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
This code is excerpted from our \c
.UR https://github.com/mdn/dom-examples/blob/main/web-speech-api/speech-color-changer/script.js
Speech color changer
.UE \c
\ example.
.PP
You can use the \f[CR]result\f[R] event in an
\f[CR]addEventListener\f[R] method:
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] recognition = \f[B]new\f[R] SpeechRecognition();

recognition.addEventListener(\(dqresult\(dq, (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  \f[B]const\f[R] color = event.results[0][0].transcript;
  diagnostic.textContent = \(gaResult received: ${color}.\(ga;
  bg.style.backgroundColor = color;
});
.EE
.PP
Or use the \f[CR]onresult\f[R] event handler property:
.IP
.EX
recognition.onresult = (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  \f[B]const\f[R] color = event.results[0][0].transcript;
  diagnostic.textContent = \(gaResult received: ${color}.\(ga;
  bg.style.backgroundColor = color;
};
.EE
